Package: bop2flex
Type: Package
Title: Sample Size Deviations in Bayesian Optimal Phase II Designs
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(
    given  = "Gosuke",
    family = "Homma",
    role   = c("aut", "cre"),
    email  = "my.name.is.gosuke@gmail.com"
  )
Description: Exact computations for the Bayesian optimal phase II design
    (BOP2) of Zhou, Lee and Yuan (2017) <doi:10.1002/sim.7338> and its
    extension with futility and efficacy stopping (BOP2-FE) of Xu, Hashimoto,
    Yimer and Takeda (2025) <doi:10.1080/10543406.2025.2558142>, for a single
    binary endpoint when the numbers of patients at the interim and final
    analyses differ from those planned. The boundaries at the actual analyses
    are derived from the error spending function implied by the planned
    design, so that the type I error rate does not exceed the nominal level
    for any sequence of analysis times chosen independently of the observed
    responses, and the planned boundaries are recovered when the trial follows
    its plan. Efficacy is never claimed with weaker posterior evidence than
    the planned final analysis requires. Planned designs can be calibrated,
    with the power or the O'Brien-Fleming type efficacy cutoff, or specified
    by their tuning parameters or boundaries. The practice of evaluating the
    planned probability cutoffs at the actual sample sizes is implemented for
    comparison. All operating characteristics are computed exactly by
    propagating the distribution of the number of responses across analyses,
    without simulation.
